1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,330
Welcome to Module 12,
all about getting paid!

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:07,983
Before Kyntlo can take a single card
payment, it needs a payment provider.

3
00:00:07,983 --> 00:00:12,887
In this lesson, we'll connect Stripe,
test it safely, and see where it's used.

4
00:00:13,737 --> 00:00:17,532
Open Payments in the sidebar,
then the Integrations tab.

5
00:00:17,532 --> 00:00:20,446
This is where every
payment provider lives.

6
00:00:20,446 --> 00:00:22,547
Stripe is the one we recommend.

7
00:00:22,547 --> 00:00:26,477
You can also connect PayPal,
Square, Authorize.net or NMI.

8
00:00:26,477 --> 00:00:31,695
Each business account connects its own
provider, so if you run two locations,

9
00:00:31,695 --> 00:00:33,593
each one is paid separately.

10
00:00:34,448 --> 00:00:38,536
Before you connect, have three
things ready: your business details,

11
00:00:38,536 --> 00:00:42,564
the bank account you want your
money paid into, and some photo ID.

12
00:00:42,564 --> 00:00:47,202
Stripe asks for these to verify your
business, and it's a legal requirement.

13
00:00:48,053 --> 00:00:50,325
Now click Connect on the Stripe card.

14
00:00:50,325 --> 00:00:52,412
Kyntlo explains what happens next.

15
00:00:52,412 --> 00:00:56,465
You'll go to Stripe, where you can
sign in to an existing account,

16
00:00:56,465 --> 00:00:58,245
or create a new one for free.

17
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:00,630
Click Connect with Stripe.

18
00:01:00,630 --> 00:01:03,933
Stripe asks you to choose the
account for this business.

19
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:08,298
Check the name and currency, pounds
for a UK business, then click Connect.

20
00:01:08,298 --> 00:01:12,722
If you're creating a brand new Stripe
account, it only takes a few minutes,

21
00:01:12,722 --> 00:01:15,435
and you'll come straight
back here afterwards.

22
00:01:16,286 --> 00:01:17,180
And that's it.

23
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:21,716
The Stripe card now says connected,
and shows the account and the mode.

24
00:01:21,716 --> 00:01:23,633
Live mode means real payments.

25
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:28,872
You can open your Stripe dashboard from
here at any time, to see payouts and fees.

26
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:31,395
So where does the money go?

27
00:01:31,395 --> 00:01:34,430
Stripe collects each
payment, takes its card fee,

28
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:38,332
and pays the rest into your bank
account on a regular schedule,

29
00:01:38,332 --> 00:01:39,756
usually every few days.

30
00:01:39,756 --> 00:01:43,720
You'll find every payout and every
fee in your Stripe dashboard,

31
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,631
and every payment in
Kyntlo's Transactions tab.

32
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,549
Want to try things out first?

33
00:01:49,549 --> 00:01:51,761
Switch on test mode at the top.

34
00:01:51,761 --> 00:01:54,329
Test payments never move real money.

35
00:01:54,329 --> 00:01:57,825
Stripe's test card number
is 4242 4242 4242 4242.

36
00:01:57,825 --> 00:02:01,036
When you're done, switch
test mode off again.

37
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:03,810
Some customers prefer PayPal.

38
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:06,195
You can connect it alongside Stripe.

39
00:02:06,195 --> 00:02:11,430
You’ll need a Client ID and Secret key
from the Apps & Credentials page of your

40
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:13,219
PayPal Developer dashboard.

41
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:15,340
Make sure you use the Live ones.

42
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:21,059
Once Stripe is connected, you can take
card payments everywhere in Kyntlo: on

43
00:02:21,059 --> 00:02:24,853
invoices, payment links and
Text2Pay, on funnel order forms,

44
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:28,015
and as deposits when someone
books an appointment.

45
00:02:28,865 --> 00:02:29,930
Here's a pro tip.

46
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:35,004
Once you're live, send yourself a £1
payment link, and pay it with your own card.

47
00:02:35,004 --> 00:02:38,950
Check it appears in Transactions
and in Stripe, then refund it.

48
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:43,334
Now you know the whole journey works,
before a customer ever tries it.

49
00:02:44,185 --> 00:02:45,919
You're ready to take payments!

50
00:02:45,919 --> 00:02:49,271
In the next lesson, we'll set
up your products and prices,

51
00:02:49,271 --> 00:02:50,832
and send our first invoice.

52
00:02:50,832 --> 00:02:51,641
See you there.
